---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';

const aiSearchFaqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between AI SEO, GEO and AEO?',
    answer: 'AI SEO is the broad term for work that helps people find a business through AI search. GEO (generative engine optimization) concentrates on generated answers. AEO (answer engine optimization) concentrates on direct answers, including search features such as featured snippets. The three overlap heavily, so we do not sell a separate service for each label. We agree the platforms to check, the pages to improve and the work you need.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does AI search optimization replace traditional SEO?',
    answer: 'No. It depends on it. Google says the same SEO fundamentals apply to AI Overviews and AI Mode, and a page that cannot be crawled or indexed is unlikely to be quoted in an AI answer. Your pages still need to be accessible, indexed and useful. We build on that work by checking what AI answers say and improving the pages buyers use to compare you.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you guarantee citations in ChatGPT, Perplexity or Google AI Overviews?',
    answer: 'No. No agency can guarantee a citation or recommendation. Each platform chooses its own sources, and answers change with the question, the location and the model. What we can do is make your business easier to describe accurately: we improve your pages and track an agreed set of questions on stated dates. Those checks are a sample and cannot cover every answer a buyer might see.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do we need an llms.txt file or special AI schema?',
    answer: 'Not for Google AI Overviews or AI Mode. Google says there is no special schema or AI text file required. Clear pages, correct structured data and crawler access matter far more than a new file format. We use valid structured data where it describes real, visible content, and we check crawler controls such as OAI-SearchBot separately for the platforms that publish them.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What does an AI search visibility audit include?',
    answer: 'We record how your business and your competitors appear for an agreed set of buyer questions, which pages get cited and whether search crawlers can reach your content. You receive a prioritized page plan listing the missing information, the technical fixes and the tracking requirements. Implementation is agreed separately, so the audit stands on its own.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you measure AI search visibility?',
    answer: 'We combine observations from the agreed prompt set with platform data where it exists: Search Console, Bing Webmaster Tools AI Performance, referral traffic and GA4 conversion events. The report keeps four things apart: a citation, a visit, a tracked action and a confirmed lead. A mention is not counted as revenue.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does AI SEO take?',
    answer: 'We set delivery dates after reviewing the site and agreeing the approvals. Search platforms then recrawl and reassess the changed pages on schedules we do not control. Our reports list completed work and observed results separately, because a page going live is not a promise of immediate citations.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much do GEO and AI SEO services cost?',
    answer: 'We provide a private proposal based on the pages, markets and technical work involved. It sets out the audit, the page edits, the implementation responsibilities and the reporting included, so you can compare the scope with your budget and with the SEO work you already pay for.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you work alongside our existing SEO team?',
    answer: 'Yes. We agree which pages we will work on, who makes the site changes and who approves them. Your team can keep implementation, or we can scope that work with you. Your subject experts review technical or regulated claims before anything is published.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Which AI assistants do you cover, and do you track share of voice?',
    answer: 'We check Google AI Overviews and AI Mode, ChatGPT search, Perplexity and Microsoft Copilot, and we agree the priority platforms for your market in the scope. For each question in the agreed set we record which businesses the answer names and which pages it cites, so you can see how often you appear beside your competitors and how that changes between checks. It is a sample of answers on stated dates. We do not present it as a market-wide share figure.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Which sectors have you published AI search reviews for?',
    answer: 'Five so far: a UK football team-management app (TeamStats), self storage (Newbury Self Store), leather goods ecommerce (Lost Dutchman Leather), bridal ecommerce (Emily Bridalwear) and a fintech software company. Each reviews an AI referral report for August 2025 to January 2026, showing which pages received AI referrals and what we recommended for them. The reviews record what each report showed; they do not attribute growth to a single edit or forecast future citations.'
  }
];

const methodSteps = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Map the questions that shape a buying decision',
    copy: 'We combine search evidence with your sales questions, product knowledge and customer objections, then group the results into discovery, comparison and selection questions. Searches we have observed stay separate from prompts we propose to test.',
    output: 'Prompt and query map'
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Check what AI answers say about you',
    copy: 'We run the agreed questions on the chosen platforms and record which businesses appear, which pages are cited and any inaccurate description of your services. Each record carries the question, the date and the market, so a later check can be compared with it.',
    output: 'Visibility baseline'
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Update the pages buyers need',
    copy: 'We compare the answers with your pages and name the exact pages and passages that need work: missing product specifications, unclear service scope, unsupported claims or content a crawler cannot reach. We agree who writes, verifies and implements each change.',
    output: 'Prioritized page work'
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    title: 'Build authority beyond the page',
    copy: 'We check the business profiles, reviews and industry publications that buyers and search systems consult. The plan lists inaccurate listings to correct and relevant opportunities for coverage, with any outreach scoped before work begins.',
    output: 'Authority plan'
  },
  {
    number: '05',
    title: 'Review answers, visits and inquiries',
    copy: 'We repeat the agreed checks, track the signals each platform exposes and connect referral visits to conversion events where the data allows. A citation is visibility. It does not become a lead or a sale until your own records say so.',
    output: 'Progress report'
  }
];

const platformRows = [
  {
    platform: 'Google',
    surface: 'AI Overviews and AI Mode',
    reality: 'Pages still need to be indexed, snippet-eligible and built on normal SEO fundamentals. Google says there is no special schema required.',
    check: 'Indexation, content usefulness, internal discovery, snippet controls and Search Console performance.'
  },
  {
    platform: 'OpenAI',
    surface: 'ChatGPT search',
    reality: 'OpenAI documents OAI-SearchBot as the crawler used to surface sites in ChatGPT search results. Search access is separate from GPTBot training controls.',
    check: 'Crawler access, cited-page quality, brand accuracy, referral traffic and priority research prompts.'
  },
  {
    platform: 'Perplexity',
    surface: 'Cited research answers',
    reality: 'Answers can cite several web sources and change between checks. We inspect the cited pages to see which information supports the answer.',
    check: 'Citation patterns, competing sources, source-page depth, evidence and freshness.'
  },
  {
    platform: 'Microsoft Copilot',
    surface: 'Copilot and Bing AI answers',
    reality: 'Bing Webmaster Tools reports citations, cited URLs and sampled grounding queries through AI Performance. These are citation records, not ranking positions.',
    check: 'AI Performance, Bing indexation, cited URLs, grounding-query themes and IndexNow suitability.'
  }
];

const geoCases = [
  { href: '/case-studies/ai-sports-saas-geo/', name: 'TeamStats', line: 'Why a team-management product page deserves a different review from football resources, and why an AI-answer sample cannot be joined to referral visits.' },
  { href: '/case-studies/ai-self-storage-geo/', name: 'Newbury Self Store', line: 'Connecting practical storage guides to accurate facility details, unit choices and a quote route without treating tracked events as inquiries.' },
  { href: '/case-studies/ai-leather-goods-ecommerce-geo/', name: 'Lost Dutchman Leather', line: 'Reading product and collection entries together, then helping shoppers compare wallet capacity, dimensions, delivery and returns.' },
  { href: '/case-studies/ai-fintech-saas-geo/', name: 'FinTech SaaS', line: 'Separating educational research, existing-user support and software evaluation before assigning commercial value to referrals.' },
  { href: '/case-studies/ai-bridal-ecommerce-geo/', name: 'Emily Bridalwear', line: 'A ball-gown category, a designer product and a lace page all appear in the report, so the review covers how each helps a shopper compare dresses and reach an appointment.' }
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="AI SEO Services Philippines | GEO & AEO | Bright Forge"
  description="AI search optimization from the Philippines for businesses buyers research before choosing. SEO, GEO and AEO with clear page improvements. Discuss your site."
  canonical="https://brightforge.com.ph/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/"
  type="service"
  faqs={aiSearchFaqs}
>
  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />

  <Hero
    badgeIcon="fas fa-comments"
    badgeText="AI SEO, GEO and AEO"
    title="AI search optimization <span>services</span>"
    breadcrumbCurrent="AI Search Optimization"
  >
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>Buyers now ask Google's AI answers, ChatGPT and similar tools which supplier to choose. Those tools draw on your website and on what other sites say about you. We check what they say about your business today, find what is missing or wrong, and improve the pages and facts those answers rely on. You receive a dated record of the answers, a page-by-page plan and a report that separates visibility from visits and inquiries.</p>
      <p>The work suits businesses that buyers research before choosing, where specifications, experience or service details decide the shortlist. We are British-led and based in the Philippines, with UK, US and Australian work. The engagement combines technical SEO, page editing and AI search monitoring, and keeps a clear route for an interested buyer to inquire.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <ButtonPrimary href="/contact/?service=ai-search-readiness#contactForm" text="Request an AI visibility audit" />
      <ButtonSecondary href="#method" text="See the method" />
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="stats">
      <div class="hero-stats">
        <div class="stat"><strong>Report reviews</strong><span>Five published, with evidence and limits</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>15+</strong><span>Years of SEO practice</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>UK US AU</strong><span>Western search work</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>GBP / USD</strong><span>Billed in buyer currency</span></div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <main class="ai-page">
    <section class="ai-proof" id="proof">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <p class="proof-people">Work led by <a href="/authors/ben-lowe/">Ben Lowe</a> and <a href="/authors/sassin-lowe/">Sassin Lowe</a>. We review the pages that explain your offer and the evidence a buyer needs before contacting you, and we publish the limits of what the data shows.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-contrast" id="buying-situations">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <div class="ai-section-heading">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> From research to a relevant inquiry</p>
          <h2>AI search work starts with <span>what your buyer needs to know</span>.</h2>
          <p>Examples of buying decisions show the work most clearly. In each of the four below, the buyer needs facts that a typical page in that sector leaves out, and our work puts them on the page. For your business, we research the market and speak with your team before choosing the questions to test.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="case-grid">
          <article class="case-card">
            <h3>Industrial suppliers</h3>
            <p>A workshop choosing an industrial parts washer has to check load capacity, material compatibility and the cleaning process. Its purchasing team also wants to know what installation and local support involve.</p>
            <p>We put verified specifications and application limits on the product page, link to the supporting documents and explain which details to send for a quote. Your technical team approves the claims.</p>
            <a href="/construction-seo-services/">Construction and industrial SEO <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
          <article class="case-card">
            <h3>Local and trade services</h3>
            <p>A homeowner needs someone to repair a leaking roof, but the contractor's page talks only about new installations. Nothing on it says whether the firm handles repairs or covers their suburb.</p>
            <p>We set out the repair services, the service area and the inspection process, add relevant completed projects and test the call or quote link. This work sits alongside Maps and Google Business Profile optimization.</p>
            <a href="/home-services-seo/">Home services SEO <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
          <article class="case-card">
            <h3>Professional services</h3>
            <p>A finance director considering outsourcing payroll wants to know who handles filings, which systems the firm supports and what happens during the handover. They need enough detail to discuss the options with colleagues before booking a consultation.</p>
            <p>We spell out the service scope and the client's responsibilities, add relevant credentials and approved examples, and explain what to bring to the first consultation. A qualified reviewer checks any regulated advice.</p>
            <a href="/b2b-seo-services/">B2B and professional-services SEO <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
          <article class="case-card">
            <h3>Ecommerce</h3>
            <p>A shopper comparing laptop bags wants to know whether their device fits, how much the bag weighs and whether the material suits a wet commute. Delivery dates and returns may decide between otherwise similar bags.</p>
            <p>We add verified internal dimensions, weight and material details, make delivery and returns easy to find, and help buyers compare suitable models. We also check that the structured product data matches the page.</p>
            <a href="/ecommerce-seo-services/">Ecommerce SEO <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-cases" id="cases">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <div class="ai-section-heading">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Report reviews</p>
          <h2>Five published reviews of <span>AI referral reports</span></h2>
          <p>These reviews use the original GEO reports for August 2025 to January 2026. Each review page states the AI referral sessions its report recorded. Together they show which pages AI tools sent visitors to, which of those pages deserve attention and how we keep referrals apart from commercial outcomes. The figures come from the reports and the recommendations are our own review findings: a clear record of what each report showed, not proof that a particular edit caused growth.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="case-grid">
          {geoCases.map((item) => (
            <a class="case-card" href={item.href}>
              <strong>{item.name}</strong>
              <p>{item.line}</p>
              <span>Read the report review</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-section" id="seo-geo-aeo">
      <div class="pf-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Three labels, one program</p>
        <h2><span>SEO, GEO and AEO</span> compared</h2>
        <p class="pf-lede">Buyers meet all three terms when they research this service. The table shows where they differ and why we scope them as one piece of work.</p>
        <div class="pf-table-wrap"><table class="pf-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">SEO</th><th scope="col">GEO</th><th scope="col">AEO</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">What it stands for</th><td>Search engine optimization</td><td>Generative engine optimization</td><td>Answer engine optimization</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Where the buyer sees you</th><td>Ranked search results</td><td>Generated answers, such as Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT search, Perplexity and Copilot</td><td>Direct answers, including search features such as featured snippets</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">What we work on</th><td>Crawling, indexing, page content, internal links and authority</td><td>The facts, specifications and evidence an answer can draw on, plus crawler access and corroborating sources</td><td>Clear questions and answers on the page that owns the topic</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">How we measure it</th><td>Search Console clicks, impressions and positions</td><td>Dated observations of an agreed question set, cited URLs and identifiable referrals</td><td>Whether the page is shown for the question, checked on stated dates</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">What nobody can promise</th><td>A ranking position</td><td>A citation or recommendation</td><td>Selection as the answer</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>
        <p class="pf-note">The three overlap, and GEO and AEO both depend on the SEO fundamentals. We agree the platforms, pages and work in one scope and do not sell a separate service for each label.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-shift">
      <div class="ai-shell ai-shift-layout">
        <div class="shift-statement">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> The commercial shift</p>
          <h2>Your next customer may meet the <em>answer</em> before they meet your website.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="shift-copy">
          <p>A buyer can ask ChatGPT to compare suppliers before visiting any of their websites. The answer may name a business, cite a product page or describe a service incorrectly. A rankings report will show you none of that.</p>
          <p>The work is often called <strong>AI SEO</strong> or <strong>generative engine optimization (GEO)</strong>. You may also see <strong>answer engine optimization (AEO)</strong> and <strong>LLM SEO</strong>. The labels overlap. What matters in practice is which platforms we check and what we change on your site.</p>
          <p>We start with the service and product pages closest to an inquiry or a purchase. Missing specifications, outdated service details and unsupported claims each give us a specific job. We then repeat the agreed checks to see whether the answers and the cited pages change.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-reality" id="reality">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <div class="ai-section-heading">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Scope and limits</p>
          <h2>What AI search optimization <span>can change</span>, and what it cannot</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reality-rule"></div>
        <div class="reality-columns">
          <div class="reality-side reality-side-positive">
            <p class="reality-label">WE CAN IMPROVE</p>
            <ul>
              <li><span>01</span><p><strong>Page access</strong>We fix the crawl barriers and internal links that make important pages hard to find.</p></li>
              <li><span>02</span><p><strong>Service information</strong>We state what you offer, where you work and which customers you can help.</p></li>
              <li><span>03</span><p><strong>Product and project detail</strong>We add verified specifications, relevant examples and current information to the pages that lack them.</p></li>
              <li><span>04</span><p><strong>Business listings and reviews</strong>We check for conflicting details and identify relevant places to build your reputation.</p></li>
              <li><span>05</span><p><strong>Reporting</strong>We show what changed on the site, what appeared in our checks and which visits led to tracked actions.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="reality-side reality-side-limit">
            <p class="reality-label">WHAT REMAINS OUTSIDE OUR CONTROL</p>
            <ul>
              <li><span>×</span><p><strong>When a platform updates</strong>Publishing an edit does not mean a platform will recrawl or use it straight away.</p></li>
              <li><span>×</span><p><strong>Inclusion in an answer</strong>Structured data can describe your pages. It cannot secure a citation or a recommendation.</p></li>
              <li><span>×</span><p><strong>Every answer a buyer sees</strong>Our question set is a sample. Answers vary by model, time, location and wording.</p></li>
              <li><span>×</span><p><strong>Untracked buying decisions</strong>A buyer may read an answer and contact you later with no identifiable referral.</p></li>
              <li><span>×</span><p><strong>How your business is described</strong>We can correct your published information and monitor the answers. The platform still chooses its wording and its sources.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-section" id="visibility-review">
      <div class="pf-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI visibility review</p>
        <h2>What the <span>AI visibility review</span> checks</h2>
        <p class="pf-lede">The review is the first piece of work and it stands on its own. To request one, <a href="/contact/?service=ai-search-readiness#contactForm">send us your website and the questions your buyers ask</a>. It covers the eight checks below.</p>
        <ul class="pf-ticks">
          <li><strong>Answers to your buyer questions.</strong> What each chosen platform says for the agreed question set, recorded with the date and market.</li>
          <li><strong>Businesses named.</strong> Whether you appear, and which competitors appear beside you.</li>
          <li><strong>Pages cited.</strong> Which of your pages, and whose pages, the answers link to.</li>
          <li><strong>Accuracy.</strong> Any wrong or outdated description of your services, products or service area.</li>
          <li><strong>Crawler access.</strong> Robots rules, rendering and indexability, including platform crawlers such as OAI-SearchBot.</li>
          <li><strong>Structured data.</strong> Whether the schema is valid and matches what is visible on the page.</li>
          <li><strong>Listings and reviews.</strong> Conflicting business details on the profiles buyers and search systems consult.</li>
          <li><strong>Tracking.</strong> Whether AI referrals and conversion events can be identified in your analytics.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-method" id="method">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <div class="method-intro">
          <div>
            <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> The Bright Forge method</p>
            <h2>From buyer questions to <span>specific page improvements</span></h2>
          </div>
          <p>Five steps, each ending in a document you keep: an agreed question set, a dated baseline, a prioritized page plan, an authority plan and a progress report. Every item of work names the person who approves it and the evidence we will use to review it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="method-ledger">
          {methodSteps.map((step) => (
            <article class="method-row">
              <span class="method-number">{step.number}</span>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.copy}</p>
              <strong>{step.output}</strong>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-source-system">
      <div class="ai-shell source-layout">
        <div class="source-copy">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Citation readiness</p>
          <h2>Make your expertise <span>easy to find and verify</span>.</h2>
          <p>A supplier specification, a named specialist, a clear returns policy or a documented project gives a buyer something to check, and gives a search system something to quote. We put that information on the page it belongs to and support it with accurate business profiles, reviews and credible third-party sources.</p>
          <p>Three services do the work. <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">Technical SEO</a> confirms that important pages can be reached and indexed. <a href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">Content SEO</a> makes the answers useful. <a href="/backlink-seo-services-philippines/">Authority work</a> supports your claims beyond your own website. Structured data then describes those visible facts. It does not replace them.</p>
          <ul class="source-layers">
            <li>Technical access</li>
            <li>Clear business information</li>
            <li>Evidence</li>
            <li>Authority</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-platforms">
      <div class="ai-shell">
        <div class="platform-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Platform-specific checks</p>
            <h2>What we check on <span>Google, ChatGPT, Perplexity and Copilot</span>.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Each platform exposes different controls and different reporting. We work from what the platforms document, then apply experienced SEO judgment where their data runs out.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="platform-run" role="table" aria-label="AI search platforms and optimization checks">
          <div class="platform-run-head" role="row">
            <span role="columnheader">Platform</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Surface</span>
            <span role="columnheader">What matters</span>
            <span role="columnheader">What we check</span>
          </div>
          {platformRows.map((row, index) => (
            <article class="platform-row" role="row">
              <div role="cell"><small>0{index + 1}</small><strong>{row.platform}</strong></div>
              <p role="cell">{row.surface}</p>
              <p role="cell">{row.reality}</p>
              <p role="cell">{row.check}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-measurement">
      <div class="ai-shell measurement-layout">
        <div class="measurement-copy">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Reporting and attribution</p>
          <h2>We separate visibility from visits, and <span>visits from leads</span>.</h2>
          <p>We report which answers cite you, which pages receive identifiable AI referrals and what those visitors do next. Each measure tells you something different about whether the work is helping, so the report keeps them in separate lines.</p>
          <p>A brand mention is not necessarily a linked citation. A citation does not prove a visit, and a conversion event does not prove a qualified inquiry. We agree what each event means and compare it with your inquiry or order records where you can share them.</p>
          <p>Search Console counts traffic from Google's AI features within its standard web-search reporting, so it cannot serve as a complete, standalone AI attribution report. Unidentified referrals and later direct visits leave further gaps, and our report states each one. For ongoing monitoring and delivery QA, see our <a href="/seo-command-centre/">SEO Command Centre</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="measurement-chain">
          <li><span>01</span><p><strong>Observed mention or citation</strong><small>We record whether an answer names the brand, links a source page or both, with the prompt, platform, market and date.</small></p></li>
          <li><span>02</span><p><strong>Cited URL or grounding query</strong><small>Where available, platform reporting shows the cited page and the queries used to find sources.</small></p></li>
          <li><span>03</span><p><strong>Referral visit</strong><small>Analytics records traffic from an identifiable AI or search surface.</small></p></li>
          <li><span>04</span><p><strong>Tracked action</strong><small>A visitor submits, calls, books or completes another configured conversion event.</small></p></li>
          <li><span>05</span><p><strong>Confirmed lead or sale</strong><small>Your commercial process confirms the outcome. Analytics alone does not.</small></p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-deliverables">
      <div class="ai-shell deliverables-layout">
        <div class="deliverables-title">
          <p class="ai-kicker"><span></span> Audit and implementation</p>
          <h2>Six deliverables in an <span>AI SEO engagement</span></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverables-list">
          <article><span>DIAGNOSE</span><h3>AI visibility and citation audit</h3><p>A dated record of what the chosen platforms answer to your agreed buyer questions: which businesses they name, which pages they cite, what they get wrong about you and which access problems need fixing.</p></article>
          <article><span>CLARIFY</span><h3>Page-by-page work plan</h3><p>For each buying question, the page that should answer it, the facts it is missing (specifications, service areas, credentials, policies) and the items that need your expert's approval before we write them.</p></article>
          <article><span>STRENGTHEN</span><h3>Revised service and product pages</h3><p>Page edits that answer the missing questions, explain comparisons and put approved evidence beside the claim it supports. The plan names who publishes each change.</p></article>
